title: Task endpoints
tags: Tasks
kind: reference
audience: dev
summary: The task JSON, listing a repository's tasks or all of them, reading one, and cancelling it.

```
{"id": "0f1e2d3c…", "repo_uuid": "aaaa…", "kind": "reconcile", "status": "running",
 "cancellable": true, "phase": "fingerprint", "done": 1240, "total": 5000,
 "started_at": "2026-06-21T11:30:00.000Z", "finished_at": null,
 "result": null, "error": null}
```

On completion, exactly one of `result` (`done`, only for the kinds whose request
did not carry the result: reconcile, duplicate scan, relink) or `error`
(`failed`). `cancellable` says whether the kind can be stopped, whatever its
status. UUIDs are 32-character lowercase hex, like everywhere in the API.

|!Endpoint |!Answers |
|<<cmd "GET /repos/:repo/tasks">> |the repository's tasks: every active one, and the finished ones still retained |
|<<cmd "GET /repos/:repo/tasks/:task">> |one task; `404` when unknown or evicted |
|<<cmd "GET /tasks">> |every loaded repository's, each carrying its `repo_uuid`: what a status display polls |
|<<cmd "POST /repos/:repo/tasks/:task/cancel">> |requests the stop ([[Cancelling a task]]) and answers the task as it stands (it may still read `running` for a moment) |

The cancel request sets the flag at once; `cancelled` appears when the worker
reaches its next checkpoint.

|!Situation |!Status |
|a cancel of an active task |`200` |
|a cancel of a finished task — nothing to stop |`409` |
|a cancel of a `load`, `prune` or `rollback` task |`400` |
|an unknown or evicted task |`404` |
|a reconcile or duplicate scan asked while one is active |`409` (the active one is in the list) |

`GET /health` stays a bare liveness check; what runs is at `GET /tasks`.
